course: dictionary
lesson: 3934
title: Frying: one word, many forms
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Frying means cooking food in hot oil or fat. «Dad is frying sausages» tells you he is cooking them in hot oil. Frying is the -ing form of the verb fry, so the word changes: fry, fries, fried, frying.
explain: Use the words around a word to find its meaning. In «the cook throws a frying-pan after her but misses», a frying pan is something you cook in. Ask: what would fit here? Then put your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Frying also works as an adjective, a word that describes a noun. A frying pan is a flat, shallow pan with a long handle, used for frying. The word pan tells you what kind of pan it is.
explain: Some words belong to phrases. «Out of the frying pan into the fire» is a saying. It means you escape one problem only to land in a worse one. It is not about real pans or real fires.
fact: Frying means cooking food in hot oil or fat.
fact: A frying pan is a flat, shallow pan with a long handle.
fact: The verb forms are fry, fries, fried and frying.
fact: Frying needs an adult, because hot oil can spit and burn.
fact: «Out of the frying pan into the fire» means escaping one problem only to land in a worse one.
exercise: «Dad is frying sausages.» What is frying? | Cutting bread into thin slices | Throwing food into the air | *Cooking food in hot oil or fat | Washing dishes in cold water
exercise: «The cook throws a frying-pan after her but misses.» What is a frying pan? | *A flat, shallow pan with a long handle | A tiny cup for tea | A deep pot with a lid for soup
exercise: What does the saying «out of the frying pan into the fire» mean? | Moving a cooker into the kitchen | Cooking dinner too quickly | *Escaping one problem only to land in a worse one | Putting out a real fire
test: «Yesterday I ___ an egg.» Choose the right form of fry. | fry | fries | frying | *fried
test: «The ___ pan was hot, so we waited.» Choose the right word. | fried | *frying | fries | fry
exam: Which statement about frying is true? | Frying means cooking food in cold water | Frying means washing food before you eat it | *Hot oil can spit and burn, so frying needs an adult | A frying pan has no handle
